## Environment gotchas (fill for this machine; delete lines that don't apply)
<!-- Recurring, turn-wasting environment traps — capture them once so no future session rediscovers them. -->
- **Windows long paths (MAX_PATH):** deeply-nested install/repo paths (e.g. a long shared-drive or scratch
  path) break pip wheels with long headers (TF/torch) and git object reads. Install heavyweight wheels into a
  SHORT root (e.g. `C:\venvs\<name>`), and set `git config --global core.longpaths true`.
- **Python launcher:** use `py -3.x` (or the venv's `python`), NOT `python3` (a Windows Store stub on many
  machines).
- **Shared-drive filesystem (Google Drive / OneDrive File Stream):** may not support symlinks/junctions
  ("Incorrect function") — use a copy/sync step instead of a symlink.
